    "body": "If this log thing is strong enough of a concern you can put the Dockerfile\nin the build repo and instruct people to clone the html repo into the build\nrepo. Just depends where you want to create pain points vs simplify the\nprocess.\n\nKind of surprised there isn't a git log command that ignores paths (maybe\nthere is); seems why change logs are curated and not just git log dumps.\n\nOn Thursday, February 4, 2016, Domenic Denicola notifications@github.com\nwrote:\n\n> @foolip https://github.com/foolip let me think harder about that... the\n> attraction of having it here is that you can just clone whatwg/html and do\n> your work entirely there. But I guess that's just an argument for merging\n> in html-build as well.\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub\n> https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/612#issuecomment-180187457.\n",
