    "created_at": "2016-02-05T04:56:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-05T04:56:25Z",
    "body": "No, it does not need to be in the root, that is just the default path where\ndocker build looks. If not in root you need to specify the path using the\n-f flag. This is pretty rare unless you have multiple dockerfiles for\ndifferent types of builds.\n\nOn Thursday, February 4, 2016, Philip Jägenstedt notifications@github.com\nwrote:\n\n> Hmm, would Dockerfile have to be in the root of the repo even with merged\n> repos?\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub\n> https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/612#issuecomment-180190072.\n",
