    "created_at": "2016-02-05T04:57:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-05T04:57:56Z",
    "body": "I think putting it in the build repo is workable, it's just kind of weird to have a big branch in the readme saying \"here are the docker instructions, here are the non-docker instructions.\" I'll try to think through tomorrow what we want to do to balance everything.\n\nThere's a separate issue of pinning to specific wattsi/html-build versions. I think this is kind of a more general problem though that dockerization just exposes to us. In general there's no way of saying, when you check out a given whatwg/html commit, what whatwg/html-build commit will work with it (master won't, for things far enough back). I guess you'd want something that correlates commit datetimes...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
