    "created_at": "2016-02-05T05:31:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-05T05:31:50Z",
    "body": "I don't think correlating the commit times would be robust, sometimes commits are pushed as-is with old committer dates (and author dates, obviously).\n\nSince it has to be an association of the type \"this html commit can be built using this html-build commit\", it has to be tracked in the html repo, or a third repo with commit-to-commit mapping. That sounds a bit crazy, merging the repos seems less bad, then.\n\nWe also have the wattsi dependency, of course. Could be tracked with a DEPS file I suppose.\n\nOr we only care about all three masters working together and say that https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/862c8b1bff2a62c0eb471ff636676a044eeef6ec will suffice for older commits?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
