    "updated_at": "2016-02-05T05:33:45Z",
    "body": "What is the issue with adding back the git reset I had in the Dockerfile?\nSeems like a simple solution to this version problem without\nover-engineering a new hack.\n\nOn Thursday, February 4, 2016, Philip Jägenstedt notifications@github.com\nwrote:\n\n> I don't think correlating the commit times would be robust, sometimes\n> commits are pushed as-is with old committer dates (and author dates,\n> obviously).\n> \n> Since it has to be an association of the type \"this html commit can be\n> built using this html-build commit\", it has to be tracked in the html repo,\n> or a third repo with commit-to-commit mapping. That sounds a bit crazy,\n> merging the repos seems less bad, then.\n> \n> We also have the wattsi dependency, of course. Could be tracked with a\n> DEPS file I suppose.\n> \n> Or we only care about all three masters working together and say that\n> https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/862c8b1bff2a62c0eb471ff636676a044eeef6ec\n> will suffice for older commits?\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub\n> https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/612#issuecomment-180206116.\n",
