    "created_at": "2016-02-05T06:09:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-05T06:09:19Z",
    "body": "I didn't follow along from the start, which git reset was that? Both wattsi and html-build are checked out at a specific commit in current Dockerfile, and that means we can't make changes to HTML that break with older versions of html-build or wattsi without also updating/testing this Dockerfile.\n\nIt'd be nice if we had an answer for \"which commits work together\" that could be applied both for vanilla html-build and this Dockerfile. Right now that answer is \"the latest commits\", but how feasible is to guarantee that here?\n\nNote that https://github.com/whatwg/html-build/pull/72 has made html-build fail by default if it's out-of-date, which I imagine will create some trouble here. Sorry :(\n",
